{"timestamp":1774883196130,"source_app":"agentic-harness","session_id":"ea373ad6-9058-4035-af35-cc4ce5d39b2e","hook_event_type":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GHUrhBtD2uARzyreLxZwqk","payload":{"session_id":"ea373ad6-9058-4035-af35-cc4ce5d39b2e","transcript_path":"/Users/rivero/.claude/projects/-Users-rivero-ai-agentic-experience-apps-mas-trees-f32e4400/ea373ad6-9058-4035-af35-cc4ce5d39b2e.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/f32e4400","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","hook_event_name":"PreToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/rivero/ai/agentic-experience/apps/mas/trees/f32e4400/specs/patch/patch-adw-11-titleclone-reactive-property.md","content":"# Patch: Make titleClone a reactive LitElement property\n\n## Metadata\nadw_id: `11`\nreview_change_request: `titleClone (mas-fragment-editor.js:423) is a plain class field not declared in static properties. The value binding value=\"${this.titleClone}\" relies on showCloneDialog triggering the re-render rather than titleClone being reactive itself. This works correctly but is an implicit dependency. Consistent with the existing tagsClone/osiClone pattern. Resolution: Either leave as-is (consistent with codebase convention) or add titleClone: { type: String, state: true } to static properties to make reactivity explicit. Severity: tech_debt`\n\n## Issue Summary\n**Original Spec:** specs/features/feat-11-prevent-duplicate-fragment-title-clone.md\n**Issue:** `titleClone` is declared as a plain class field at line 423 and not listed in `static properties`, meaning LitElement does not treat it as a reactive property. The template binding `value=\"${this.titleClone}\"` currently only re-renders because `showCloneDialog` (which is reactive) changes at the same time. This implicit coupling is fragile and inconsistent with how similar fields should be managed.\n**Solution:** Add `titleClone: { type: String, state: true }` to `static properties` to make reactivity explicit, matching the LitElement pattern already used for all other dialog-related state fields.\n\n## Files to Modify\n- `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`\n\n## Implementation Steps\n\n### Step 1: Add titleClone to static properties\n- In `static properties` (line 380\u2013392), add `titleClone: { type: String, state: true }` alongside the other clone/dialog state fields.\n\n### Step 2: Remove the redundant plain class field initializer\n- At line 423, `titleClone = '';` is now declared as both a static property default (LitElement handles initialization to `''` implicitly via the `String` type) and a class field. Remove the class field declaration to eliminate the duplicate.\n  - Note: LitElement initializes reactive properties to `undefined` unless a `hasChanged` default is set \u2014 keep `titleClone = '';` as the class field initializer to preserve the empty-string default, but the `static properties` entry is what makes it reactive. Both can coexist; only the `static properties` entry needs to be added.\n\n## Validation\nExecute every command to validate the patch is complete with zero regressions.\n\n1. `node --check studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js` \u2014 verify syntax is valid after the change\n2. `grep -n \"titleClone\" studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js` \u2014 confirm entry appears in both `static properties` and as the class field initializer\n3. `grep -n \"type: String, state: true\" studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js` \u2014 confirm the property descriptor is well-formed\n\n## Patch Scope\n**Lines of code to change:** 1 (one new line added to `static properties` block)\n**Risk level:** low\n**Testing required:** Syntax check only; no behavioral change \u2014 re-render behavior is identical, only the reactivity contract becomes explicit.\n"},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GHUrhBtD2uARzyreLxZwqk"}}
